# Quillback

## Lore

Quillbacks are small, wiry humanoids of the Baalgor Wastelands, coated in a dense pelt of porcupine quills that runs from pale gray to dull brown, with a rodent''s snout and lean, sinewy limbs. Nearly everything bigger than a Quillback wants to eat it, and the race gets by on quick wits, quicker feet and the quills.

They keep no tribes and no homes. A pair courts, raises a litter of kits for a few months and parts for good; the young scatter before their first year is out. Loose bands called hutches, two to ten strong, travel together for safety and seldom last more than a year or two. Quillbacks know each other by scent, so old friends are recognized at once, and a reunion means days of eating, drinking, dancing and stories. The best stories are funny and exciting with just a touch of sorrow in them, because Quillbacks bury friends often.

Every Quillback is a pack rat. Looks decide value for them and material does not, so a sparkling stone is likely to be picked over a magic blade that has gone dull. Those who spend time among the "tall folk" learn what others value and collect it to trade for the trinkets they really want. They are not thieves by nature, but they covet badly and tend to "borrow" and forget; roughly one in ten is a habitual thief or a kleptomaniac.

**Alignment:** Mostly unprincipled or anarchist. A few are scrupulous, miscreant or aberrant, and those are rare.

**O.C.C.s available:** Any man at arms except Long Bowman, Knight and Palladin; clergy, psychics, vagabonds and entertainers; or the Quillback Scavenger R.C.C. No men of magic.

**Size:** Four to five feet tall. **Weight:** 75 to 100 pounds (35-45 kg).

**Average Life Span:** 15 to 20 years in the wild, where a Quillback past 10 is old. In a town or city one can reach 50 or 60.

**Habitat:** The Rocky Desert and the forests of the Baalgor Mountains. Merchants and slavers have lately carried them to the Western Empire, the Land of the South Winds and the Yin-Sloth Jungles.

**Languages:** A chittering dialect of Gobblely; many pick up Elven, Giantese and Western Human.

## GM Notes

Anything larger than a Quillback is feared until it proves itself, above all Baalizad, Gromek, giants, orcs, ogres, trolls and some humans, elves and dwarves. Friends are whoever has earned trust: usually Eandroth, Dragonmen, Vrill and some Quorians, Gosai, humans, elves and dwarves. Small size alone wins a Quillback''s confidence, so gnomes and faeries get it immediately whatever their alignment; faeries in particular have made Quillbacks pay for that.

The quills cut both ways at the table. They are free armor and a free weapon, and they rule out worn armor and clothing altogether. The "borrowing" habit is a mild nuisance inside a party and a real danger in a town with a watch.
